          "say": "In minus x to the 5 plus four x cubed, the leading coefficient is minus 1.",
          "write": "−x⁵ + 4x³: lead coeff −1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Function notation P(x)",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "We name a polynomial P of x. P of 2 means replace every x with 2.",
          "write": "P(x) = 2x³ − 3x² + x − 5"
        },
        {
          "say": "Two times 8, minus three times 4, plus 2, minus 5. That's 1.",
          "write": "P(2) = 16 − 12 + 2 − 5 = 1"
        },
        {
          "say": "For P of minus 1, use brackets. Minus 1 cubed is minus 1.",
          "write": "P(−1) = −2 − 3 − 1 − 5 = −11"
        },
        {
          "say": "P of 0 is always the constant term.",
          "write": "P(0) = constant"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Adding and multiplying",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "To add or subtract, collect like terms with the same power.",
          "write": "like terms: same power"
        },
        {
          "say": "When subtracting a bracket, change the sign of every term inside.",
          "write": "−(x³ + 4x² − 7) = −x³ − 4x² + 7"
        },
        {
          "say": "To multiply, every term times every term.",
          "write": "(x + 2)(x² − 3x + 4)"
        },
        {
          "say": "x times each term, then 2 times each term.",
          "write": "x³ − 3x² + 4x + 2x² − 6x + 8"
        },
        {
          "say": "Collect like terms.",
          "write": "x³ − x² − 2x + 8"
        },
        {
          "say": "Degrees add when you multiply. Degree 1 times degree 2 gives degree 3.",
          "write": "1 + 2 = 3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "A box's volume",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A box has height x, width x plus 1, and length x plus 3.",
          "write": "V = x(x + 1)(x + 3)",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y10/maths/introducing-polynomials-box.svg",
          "alt": "Box with sides x, x + 1 and x + 3"
        },
        {
          "say": "Expand two brackets first.",
          "write": "(x + 1)(x + 3) = x² + 4x + 3"
        },
        {
          "say": "Then multiply by x.",
          "write": "V(x) = x³ + 4x² + 3x"
        },
        {
          "say": "V of 2 is 8 plus 16 plus 6, which is 30 cubic centimetres.",
          "write": "V(2) = 30 cm³"
        }
      ]
    },
